@@ -688,7 +688,7 @@
     "overview": "Suthie Care is a working ledger for people who have to call someone back today. The page is a grey canvas carrying white work surfaces; inside them, information is ruled by 1px lines rather than boxed into tinted panels, numbers sit in tabular columns, and the only loud thing on screen is risk. The brand orange survives from the original app, but it has been split in two: a bright decorative orange that marks selection and progress, and a darker burnt action orange that carries white text at AA contrast.\n\nDensity is calm and operational, not dashboard-busy. A queue row shows a name, a case code, a risk pill and a status pill, and nothing else competes with them. Detail opens beside the list as a right-hand drawer, so staff never lose their place, and the drawer walks the follow-up as numbered steps. Phones get the same workflow, not a summary: rows become cards, the drawer goes full-screen, and every control grows to a 44px target.\n\nPrivacy is visual policy. Names, phone numbers and national IDs appear masked by default; dates appear in the Buddhist era. Neither is a styling choice to revisit per screen.",
     "keyCharacteristics": [
       "Grey canvas, white cards, 1px dividers; tint is for state, not for grouping.",
